+
+Memory runs now accept `--renderer=both|catalog|processing` (default both).
+Catalog mode exercises public AppDataGrid at page50/page200, using its native
+selection label and sort menu; processing retains the selector/portal workload.
+Each renderer/workload has its own receipt and heap snapshot names. Native label
+activation is followed by an exact checked-state assertion; visually hidden
+checkbox inputs are not used as pointer targets. The disposal checks include the
+fixture's zero owned intervals/animation frames and unmounted state, alongside
+existing root/scope/portal and delayed-publication assertions. These counters
+remain bounded ownership evidence, not a global listener census or heap guarantee.
+
+The deterministic private-host controller tests need no browser or build:
+`node --test --test-concurrency=1 apps/docs/scripts/grid-host-operation.test.mjs`
+from the repository root on supported Node24. Latency and GC-instrumented memory
+runs remain separate coordinator jobs against an immutable production preview.
